IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-s22-25-goods`
IMPORT `theft-s34-interpretation`

-- Theft Act 1968 ss 22 to 25: tests. Layer 1.
-- Expected values were written by hand from the text of the section named beside
-- them. Yes/no fields of a fixture are FALSE unless the fixture's name says
-- otherwise.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Expected penalties`

GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected fourteen years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 14)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected summary level 3 fine only` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `the section states no imprisonment`
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected ten years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 10)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected three years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 3)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

§§ `Goods (s 24)`

`goods stolen in England` MEANS `Goods facts` WITH
    `where the goods came from` IS `the goods originally stolen, or parts of them`
    `they are land, or a thing forming part of land that has not been severed from it by stealing` IS FALSE
    `the stealing, or the blackmail, was an offence under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the stealing, or the blackmail, amounted to an offence where and when it happened` IS FALSE
    `the fraud amounted to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS FALSE
    `the money, or the part of it asked about, derives from the wrongful credit` IS FALSE
    `they have been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS FALSE
    `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft` IS FALSE
