§§ `Wrongful credits (s 24A)`

`wc bank, from theft` MEANS `Wrongful credit facts` WITH
    `a credit of an amount of money has been made to an account` IS TRUE
    `the credit is of money in a currency other than sterling` IS FALSE
    `the account is kept by him, or he has a right or interest in it` IS TRUE
    `the account is kept with a bank` IS TRUE
    `the account is kept with a business in the course of which money received by way of deposit is lent to others` IS FALSE
    `the account is kept with a business another activity of which is financed wholly or to a material extent out of the capital of or the interest on money received by way of deposit` IS FALSE
    `the account is kept with an electronic money issuer within paragraphs (a) to (j) of the definition in regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS FALSE
    `the account was overdrawn before or after the credit was made` IS FALSE
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from theft` IS TRUE
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from blackmail` IS FALSE
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from fraud contrary to section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS FALSE
    `the credit derives, at least in part, from stolen goods` IS FALSE
    `he knows or believes that the credit is wrongful` IS TRUE
    `he failed to take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to secure that the credit is cancelled` IS TRUE
    `dishonest in failing to take those steps` IS TRUE
